    "lines": [
     {
      "kind": "bullet",
      "text": "**Pulling the full player down is smooth now, including the first time.** 1.3.8 made each frame of the pull cheaper, but not enough. The player was Kultr's own card drawn over the app. On every frame of the pull, Kultr redrew the card, cut it to shape, shrank it, and redrew the glass tab bar under it. The phone couldn't keep up, so the first pull jumped and paused, and every pull moved at 30 frames a second. The player is now an iOS sheet, and iOS moves it by itself at the screen's full frame rate. Pull down from the top of the player to close it; if you've scrolled down to the queue, the list scrolls back up first."
